---
import Layout from '../components/Layout.astro';
import { systems, converters } from '../data/systems';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<Layout title="About — Ancient Numbers" active="about">
  <div class="container">
    <article class="about-page">
      <h1>About</h1>
      <p class="about-intro">
        Ancient Numbers covers {systems.length} numeral and counting traditions, including modern
        and living systems.
      </p>
      <h2>Notation</h2>
      <p>
        Each entry identifies its period, variant, and sources. Numerals use vector drawings with
        consistent weight and spacing. Some complex forms adapt openly licensed font outlines;
        credits and licenses are included in SVG downloads.
      </p>
      <h2>Limits</h2>
      <p>
        There are {converters.length} converters, each with an explicit supported range. Supported
        ranges are app limits unless stated otherwise. Number words, knots, and body counting use
        words or diagrams. Place-value labels and diagram guides are modern reading aids.
      </p>
      <h2>Calculations</h2>
      <p>
        Decimals and fractions are calculated exactly. If a system cannot display the result, the
        answer remains visible in familiar digits. The calculator explains number formation and
        includes worked applications of documented methods, such as Egyptian doubling and Babylonian
        reciprocal division. Sources distinguish historical procedures from modern teaching examples
        and translations of an equation.
      </p>
      <h2>Code</h2>
      <p>
        The app runs in your browser with no accounts or tracking. Original code and artwork use the
        MIT license; adapted artwork retains its original license.
      </p>
      <a class="inline-link" href="https://github.com/CumputerSluts/ancient-numbers">
        GitHub <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
      </a>
      <h2 id="sources">Sources</h2>
      <p>Each system page links to references for its notation and examples.</p>
      <ul class="about-source-index">
        {[...systems]
          .sort((a, b) => a.name.localeCompare(b.name))
          .map((s) => (
            <li>
              <a href={`${base}systems/${s.id}/`}>{s.name} ↗</a>
              <small>{s.sources[0].title}</small>
            </li>
          ))}
      </ul>
      <h2>Corrections</h2>
      <p>Submit corrections or new systems through GitHub. Include an example and a source.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</Layout>
